# The golden conformance vectors are the byte-exact cross-language contract that
# Python, .NET, and Unity are all replayed against. Git must never rewrite them.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows (where Git's default is core.autocrlf=true)
# silently converts every text vector's LF to CRLF on checkout. The binary
# vectors survive — git detects the NUL bytes — but the .rle patterns do not,
# and the RLE conformance tests then fail against their own corrupted fixtures.
# The failure reads as "the implementation is wrong" when in fact the checkout
# is; that inversion is exactly what the determinism contract cannot afford.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion in both directions, so the bytes on
# disk are the bytes in the blob on every platform.
vectors/** -text

# Same reasoning for pattern fixtures shipped inside the Unity package's tests.
*.rle -text
